From: Freifunk im Neanderland <projekt@neanderfunk.de>
Subject: ag71xx: do not BUG() when the RX ring runs out of refilled buffers

On a TP-Link Archer C25 v1 (64 MB, ath9k + ath10k) under memory pressure
the RX refill in ag71xx_ring_rx_refill() fails (napi_alloc_frag), and once
every descriptor has been consumed the RX loop hits ag71xx_assert(0):

  eth0: out of memory
  drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c,1317: assertion failed
  Kernel bug detected[#1]:  ... Comm: kswapd0
  Call Trace: BUG <- ag71xx_poll <- __napi_poll <- net_rx_action <- ...
  Kernel panic - not syncing: Fatal exception in interrupt

The driver already has a recovery path for exactly this case: after the
RX loop, ag71xx_poll() finds the buffer at ring->dirty missing, prints
"out of memory", completes NAPI and arms oom_timer, which reschedules NAPI
to retry the refill. The assertion fires one step earlier and turns a
temporary allocation failure into a reboot loop (about every 3 minutes on
the C25).

Break out of the loop instead, with a rate-limited warning, and let the
existing OOM path retry. While the ring is empty the MAC drops frames and
reports an RX overflow, which ag71xx_poll() already handles by restarting
RX once buffers are back.

Signed-off-by: Freifunk im Neanderland <projekt@neanderfunk.de>
---
--- a/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
+++ b/drivers/net/ethernet/atheros/ag71xx/ag71xx_main.c
@@ -1314,7 +1314,14 @@
 			break;
 
 		if ((ring->dirty + ring_size) == ring->curr) {
-			ag71xx_assert(0);
+			/* Every descriptor went to the stack and none could be
+			 * refilled: the page allocator failed in
+			 * ag71xx_ring_rx_refill(). Stop here instead of BUG().
+			 * ag71xx_poll() then takes its out-of-memory path and
+			 * retries the refill from oom_timer.
+			 */
+			net_warn_ratelimited("%s: RX ring exhausted, waiting for refill\n",
+					     dev->name);
 			break;
 		}
 
